== 1. all 256 bytes: size of each priority (tie) class ==
  priority 0:  64 bytes tie
  priority 1:  32 bytes tie
  priority 2:  16 bytes tie
  priority 3:   8 bytes tie
  priority 4:   4 bytes tie
  priority 5:   2 bytes tie
  priority 6:   1 bytes tie
  priority 7: 129 bytes tie
  distinct bytes that tie pairwise: 10923 of 32640 pairs

== 2. the law discards every bit above the lowest set evidence bit ==
  rank(x) == rank(x & -x) for all 1<=x<128: True
  evidence bits set but not read across the 127 evidenced bytes: 321

== 3. bytes the BODY can construct today (guard.rank_observations) ==
  FAILONLY never measured (docstring), RETRIED never passed by a caller
  reachable bytes: 64; priorities reachable: [0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
  priority 0:  32 reachable bytes tie
  priority 2:  16 reachable bytes tie
  priority 3:   8 reachable bytes tie
  priority 4:   4 reachable bytes tie
  priority 5:   2 reachable bytes tie
  priority 6:   1 reachable bytes tie
  priority 7:   1 reachable bytes tie
  priority 1 (FAILONLY) reachable: False
  priority 7 reachable only by the all-zero byte: True

== 4. bytes under the MechanicalObserver (SIGNALED always 1) ==
  observers.py:39-40 emits an Observation only `if kinds:` -> SIGNALED=1
  reachable bytes: 32; priorities reachable: [0, 2, 3]
  priority 0:  16 bytes tie
  priority 2:   8 bytes tie
  priority 3:   8 bytes tie
  RECENT/CHEAP/DENSE never change the priority when SIGNALED=1: True
  concrete ties (same priority, different evidence):
    p=0: FRAME+SIGNALED  ==  FRAME+NAMED+SIGNALED+RECENT+CHEAP+DENSE
    p=2: NAMED+SIGNALED  ==  NAMED+SIGNALED+RECENT+CHEAP+DENSE
    p=3: SIGNALED  ==  SIGNALED+RECENT+CHEAP+DENSE

== 5. monotone but not strict: adding evidence can only tie or improve ==
  bit additions that improve priority: 127
  bit additions that leave it tied:    321

== 6. the tie-break the body uses is not in the byte ==
  guard.py:411-427 key = (rank(byte), -shared_name_tokens, incoming index)
  shared_name_tokens is a DEGREE of NAMED; the law reads NAMED as 0/1 only
  incoming index = Packet.lines order = ascending line number (localize.py:38)
